Table full name: bigquery-public-data.nhtsa_traffic_fatalities.vehicle_2015
Column name: consecutive_number Type: INT64 Description: This data element is the unique case number assigned to each crash. It appears on each data file and is used to merge information from the data files together. xxxxxx Two Characters for State Code followed by Four Characters for Case Number
Column name: hour_of_crash Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the hour at which the crash occurred.0-23 Hour -- Not Applicable or Not Notified 99 Unknown
Column name: first_harmful_event Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the first injury or damage producing event of the crash. For more info on the codes, please look at C19 First Harmful Event section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: manner_of_collision Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the orientation of two motor vehicles in-transport when they are involved in the “First Harmful Event” of a collision crash. If the “First Harmful Event” is not a collision between two motor vehicles in-transport it is classified as such. For more info on the codes, please look at C20 Manner of Collision section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: body_type Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies a classification of this vehicle based on its general body configuration, size, shape, doors, etc. For more info on the codes, please look at V11 Body Type section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: travel_speed Type: INT64 Description: This data element records the speed the vehicle was traveling prior to the occurrence of the crash as reported by the investigating officer. 000 Stopped Motor Vehicle in Transport 001-151 Reported Speed Up to 151 mph -- Speed Greater than 96 mph 997 Speed Greater than 151 mph 998 Not Reported 999 Unknown
Column name: rollover Type: STRING Description: This data element identifies this vehicle’s involvement in a rollover or overturn during the crash. Rollover is defined as any vehicle rotation of 90 degrees or more about any true longitudinal or lateral axis. Rollover can occur at any time during the crash. 0 No Rollover -- First Event 1 Rollover, Tripped by Object/Vehicle -- Subsequent Event 2 Rollover, Untripped 9 Rollover, Unknown Type
Column name: extent_of_damage Type: STRING Description: This data element records the amount of damage sustained by this vehicle as indicated in the case materials based on an operational damage scale. 0 No Damage 2 Minor Damage 4 Functional Damage 6 Disabling Damage 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: vehicle_removal Type: STRING Description: This data element describes the mode by which this vehicle left the scene of the crash. -- Driven Away -- Towed Away 2 Towed Due to Disabling Damage -- Abandoned/Left Scene 3 Towed Not Due to Disabling Damage -- Not Towed Away -- Abandoned/Left at Scene 5 Not Towed 8 Not Reported 9 Unknown
Column name: most_harmful_event Type: INT64 Description: This data element describes the event that resulted in the most severe injury or, if no injury, the greatest property damage involving this vehicle. For more info on the codes, please look at V32 Most Harmful Event section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: speeding_related Type: STRING Description: This data element records whether the driver's speed was related to the crash as indicated by law enforcement. 0 No -- Yes 2 Yes, Racing 3 Yes, Exceeded Speed Limit 4 Yes, Too Fast for Conditions 5 Yes, Specifics Unknown 8 No Driver Present/Unknown if Driver Present 9 Unknown
Column name: roadway_surface_condition Type: INT64 Description: This data element identifies the attribute that best represents the roadway surface condition prior to this vehicle’s critical precrash event. For more info on the codes, please look at PC11 Roadway Surface Condition section in the pdf: https://crashstats.nhtsa.dot.gov/Api/Public/ViewPublication/812315
Column name: driver_drinking Type: STRING Description: This data element records whether the driver was drinking and is derived from data elements in the Vehicle and Person data files. 0 No Drinking 1 Drinking -- Unknown
Sample rows:
[{'consecutive_number': 240247, 'hour_of_crash': 17, 'first_harmful_event': 12, 'manner_of_collision': 6, 'body_type': 14, 'travel_speed': 998, 'rollover': 'No Rollover', 'extent_of_damage': 'Disabling Damage', 'vehicle_removal': 'Towed Due to Disabling Damage', 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'speeding_related': 'Yes, Too Fast for Conditions', 'roadway_surface_condition': 2, 'driver_drinking': 'Drinking'}, {'consecutive_number': 470149, 'hour_of_crash': 23, 'first_harmful_event': 12, 'manner_of_collision': 6, 'body_type': 14, 'travel_speed': 998, 'rollover': 'No Rollover', 'extent_of_damage': 'Disabling Damage', 'vehicle_removal': 'Towed Due to Disabling Damage', 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'speeding_related': 'No', 'roadway_surface_condition': 2, 'driver_drinking': 'Drinking'}, {'consecutive_number': 80369, 'hour_of_crash': 15, 'first_harmful_event': 12, 'manner_of_collision': 6, 'body_type': 14, 'travel_speed': 998, 'rollover': 'No Rollover', 'extent_of_damage': 'Disabling Damage', 'vehicle_removal': 'Towed Due to Disabling Damage', 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'speeding_related': 'Unknown', 'roadway_surface_condition': 1, 'driver_drinking': 'No Drinking'}, {'consecutive_number': 320119, 'hour_of_crash': 15, 'first_harmful_event': 12, 'manner_of_collision': 6, 'body_type': 2, 'travel_speed': 94, 'rollover': 'No Rollover', 'extent_of_damage': 'Disabling Damage', 'vehicle_removal': 'Towed Due to Disabling Damage', 'most_harmful_event': 12, 'speeding_related': 'Yes, Exceeded Speed Limit', 'roadway_surface_condition': 1, 'driver_drinking': 'No Drinking'}, {'consecutive_number': 470078, 'hour_of_crash': 9, 'first_harmful_event': 42, 'manner_of_collision': 0, 'body_type': 2, 'travel_speed': 998, 'rollover': 'No Rollover', 'extent_of_damage': 'Disabling Damage', 'vehicle_removal': 'Towed Due to Disabling Damage', 'most_harmful_event': 42, 'speeding_related': 'No', 'roadway_surface_condition': 1, 'driver_drinking': 'No Drinking'}]

